<title>TURKMENISTAN: Turkmen Feb cotton output down 58.8 pct vs Jan.</title>
<headline>Turkmen Feb cotton output down 58.8 pct vs Jan.</headline>
<dateline>ASHGABAT 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turkmenistan's output of cotton fibre fell by 58.8 percent to 5,600 tonnes in February compared with the previous month, the State Statistics Committee said on Monday.</p>
<p>    TURKMEN COTTON OUTPUT	Feb '97   Jan '97   Jan-Feb '97</p>
<p>     (thousand tonnes)	     5,600    13,600	19,200</p>
<p>    Month-on-month pct change    -58.8    -35.2	   n/a</p>
<p>    Year-on-year pct change	  n/a    -61.4	 -69.3</p>
<p>Around 90 percent of Turkmen cotton fibre is exported to Hong Kong, Turkey, Switzerland, Great Britain, Sweden, Pakistan, Austria and Bulgaria.</p>
<p>--Almaty Newsroom +7 3272 509410</p>
</text>
